0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 6, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The spec is implemented and its check passes: the command it lists gives **463 passed, 4 skipped**. The implementer also reported that the full suite passes (1186 passed, 16 skipped), but I didn't run that myself.\n\nAll the changes are in `sqlite_utils/db.py`. I read the full diff against the spec and it matches section by section: the new `ForeignKey` dataclass and `_fk_actions_sql`, reading compound keys and actions back from the database, `resolve_foreign_keys`, `create_table_sql`, `add_foreign_keys`, `index_foreign_keys`, `transform`/`transform_sql`, and `add_foreign_key`. Nothing else in the package still unpacks `ForeignKey` as a tuple, which would now raise an error. The test files are unchanged.\n\n`black` and `mypy` aren't installed in the venv, so formatting and type checks haven't been run.\n\nThe implementer made three choices the spec doesn't cover:\n- **Mismatched column counts:** `add_foreign_keys` raises `ValueError` when a 4-tuple has a different number of columns on each side.\n- **Index matching:** `index_foreign_keys` now compares whole column tuples, as the spec asks. As a result, a single-column key whose only index is a composite one starting with that column now gets its own index; before, it didn't.\n- **Type hint:** `drop_foreign_keys` is now typed `Iterable[Any]` so it accepts tuples of column names.\n\nNothing has been committed.", "ttft_ms": 2770, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 263141, "uuid": "09354c17-8302-4a19-a6ba-fdb0f4499271", "ttft_stream_ms": 2396, "time_to_request_ms": 669, "first_content_frame_ms": 2396, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
